# Tests that cannot run inside the Nix build sandbox, with the reason for each.
#
# These tests are NOT broken and NOT skipped locally — `bin/run_test_suite` runs
# every one of them on a real machine, and the pre-push gate requires them green.
# They are excluded only from `checks.<system>.test`, the hermetic flake check
# that Mechatron builds, because the sandbox deliberately has no network, no
# hardware access, no terminal, no user account, and none of the sibling
# repositories under ~/Code.
#
# The flake prints this list and its count on every run, so the exclusion is
# visible in the CI log rather than implied by a smaller number.
#
# Format: one test file name per line, '#' comments ignored. Keep the reason
# attached to the entry. Removing an entry is a deliberate diff — that is the
# point: it is how a test graduates to being hermetic.

# ── Requires a real terminal, tmux server, or interactive session ────────────
shell_startup_test

# ── Requires the user's live system configuration or account layout ──────────
# pathconfig asserts NixOS wrapper ordering under /run/wrappers.
pathconfig_bash_prepend_test
# block-attribution validates the installed global Claude hook, which is owned
# outside this repository and intentionally absent from the sandbox fixture.
block-attribution_test
